From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] DiscDirectoryHelper: keep a Blu-ray's resume point when its playlist is found for it

A Blu-ray the scan could not resolve to a playlist stays in the library as
its index.bdmv or its image. To play it, GetOrShowPlaylistSelection()
finds the playlist and points the item and its tag at the bluray:// path
of it. When the item stops, CSaveFileState keeps the resume point against
that path and moves the library entry to it, so the next play finds both.
It moves the entry only when the tag's path differs from the played one,
or when new_playlist_path says the playlist changed; the tag was already
pointed at the playlist, so that leaves the flag.

The flag was set only for a playlist the user picked from the menu. One
found without asking - the main title, as the "play main title" setting
does at every start - left the entry on index.bdmv while the resume point
went to the playlist, which nothing looks up: a film stopped at 20:00
started from the beginning again.

A playlist found without asking now sets the flag too when the item came
as a disc image or folder. An item already on a bluray:// playlist keeps
its link: the main title, found from the disc's root, need not be the
playlist the user or an nfo chose for it, and moving the entry would lose
that choice for good.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/filesystem/DiscDirectoryHelper.cpp b/xbmc/filesystem/DiscDirectoryHelper.cpp
index b7590c888f..d9185940e2 100644
--- a/xbmc/filesystem/DiscDirectoryHelper.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/filesystem/DiscDirectoryHelper.cpp
@@ -4084,8 +4084,18 @@ bool CDiscDirectoryHelper::GetOrShowPlaylistSelection(const CFileItem& item,
     items.Add(newItem);
   }
   else if (!returnMultipleItems)
+  {
     // Return single item
-    items.Add(GenerateItem(item, *sourceItems[0]));
+    const auto newItem{GenerateItem(item, *sourceItems[0])};
+
+    // A playlist found for a disc image or folder is as much a change as one the user
+    // picked; an item already on a playlist keeps it
+    if (!URIUtils::IsBlurayPath(item.GetDynPath()) &&
+        sourceItems[0]->GetDynPath() != item.GetDynPath())
+      newItem->SetProperty("new_playlist_path", true);
+
+    items.Add(newItem);
+  }
   else
   {
     // Return all items
